==Tok Pisin==

===Etymology===
Cognate to {{cog|bi|bensin||petrol}} (a term which entered Bislama before 1885). According to Terry Crowley, the term derives either from {{bor|tpi|de|Benzin}}, or from {{bor|tpi|en|benzene}}, as the meaning of that term was not as narrow or technical in the nineteenth century as it is today.<ref>Terry Crowley, ''Beach-la-Mar to Bislama: the emergence of a national language in Vanuatu'' (1990), page 137.</ref>

